---
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';
import ToolingStack from '../components/ToolingStack.astro';
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';

const [featuredWork] = (await getCollection('work'))
  .sort((a, b) => a.data.order - b.data.order)
  .filter((entry) => entry.data.featured);

const featuredStrengths = [
  {
    title: 'Backend systems and architecture',
    body: 'APIs, domain modeling, data flow, and system design that scale without becoming fragile.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Production reliability',
    body: 'Observability, failure handling, recovery paths, and delivery discipline under real load.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Event-driven workflows',
    body: 'Systems designed so operational events trigger downstream actions cleanly.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Workflow orchestration',
    body: 'Automation using webhooks, background jobs, and tools like n8n as part of system design.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Applied AI systems',
    body: 'Summaries, classification, analytics explanation, and decision support grounded in real data.',
  },
];

const signalCards = [
  {
    kicker: 'Current work',
    title: featuredWork.data.title,
    body: featuredWork.data.summary,
  },
  {
    kicker: 'About',
    title: 'Systems engineering first',
    body: 'My foundation is backend systems, APIs, infrastructure, data flow, and product architecture. The automation and AI layer sits on top of that foundation, not instead of it.',
  },
  {
    kicker: 'Applied AI',
    title: 'Operational use, not hype',
    body: 'I use AI where it helps real systems: summaries, classification, routing, and operational visibility tied to actual workflows and data.',
  },
];
---

<SiteLayout
  title="Jariel Balberona | Senior Software Engineer and AI Automation Engineer"
  description="Jariel Balberona builds production-grade systems, event-driven workflows, automation infrastructure, and AI-assisted operational tools."
  activeNav="home"
>
  <section class="mb-20">
    <p class="mb-5 text-xs font-mono uppercase tracking-widest text-ink-soft">Senior software engineer and AI automation engineer</p>
    <h1 class="max-w-[14ch] text-4xl sm:text-5xl lg:text-6xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink leading-tight">
      I build production-grade systems, event-driven workflows, and AI-assisted operational tools.
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-6 max-w-2xl text-lg leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
      I design backend systems, APIs, and data flows that hold up under real operational pressure, then extend them with automation and AI to reduce manual work and improve system clarity.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl text-base leading-relaxed text-ink">
      Current focus is Dumadine, a multi-tenant hospitality operating system evolving into an event-driven platform with automation workflows, reporting systems, and AI-assisted operational support.
    </p>
    <div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap gap-4">
      <a href="/work" class="inline-flex bg-ink px-5 py-2.5 text-sm font-medium text-paper no-underline hover:bg-ink-soft transition-colors">See selected work</a>
      <a href="/workflow" class="inline-flex border border-line px-5 py-2.5 text-sm font-medium text-ink no-underline hover:border-ink hover:text-ink transition-colors">Read my workflow</a>
    </div>
    <p class="mt-8 max-w-2xl text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
      Core strengths: backend architecture, system design, event-driven workflows, platform reliability, and operational tooling that stays useful beyond the demo.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="mb-20 grid gap-8 md:grid-cols-3">
    {
      signalCards.map((card) => (
        <article class="border-t border-line pt-5">
          <p class="mb-3 text-xs font-mono uppercase tracking-widest text-ink-soft">{card.kicker}</p>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink">{card.title}</h2>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">{card.body}</p>
        </article>
      ))
    }
  </section>

  <section class="mb-20 border-t border-line pt-10">
    <p class="mb-3 text-xs font-mono uppercase tracking-widest text-ink-soft">About</p>
    <h2 class="max-w-2xl text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink leading-tight">Systems first. Automation and AI where they actually matter.</h2>
    <p class="mt-5 max-w-2xl text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
      I have spent the last 9 years building production systems across backend architecture, APIs, infrastructure, and data-heavy workflows.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-5 max-w-2xl text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
      My foundation is still systems engineering: defining boundaries, handling failure, designing data flow, and building software that remains maintainable as complexity grows.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-5 max-w-2xl text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
      The extension layer is automation and applied AI. I focus on systems that reduce manual coordination, surface meaningful operational signals, explain system behavior, and support faster, better decisions.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-5 max-w-2xl text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
      I am not interested in AI as branding. I use it where it improves real workflows: summaries, classification, routing, and operational visibility.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="mb-20 border-t border-line pt-10">
    <p class="mb-3 text-xs font-mono uppercase tracking-widest text-ink-soft">Key strengths</p>
    <h2 class="max-w-2xl text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink leading-tight">Shipping once is easy. Keeping the system usable after that is the real work.</h2>
    <div class="mt-10 grid gap-8 md:grid-cols-2 md:gap-12">
      {
        featuredStrengths.map((item) => (
          <div>
            <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink">{item.title}</h3>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">{item.body}</p>
          </div>
        ))
      }
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mb-20 border-t border-line pt-10">
    <p class="mb-3 text-xs font-mono uppercase tracking-widest text-ink-soft">Automation and AI systems</p>
    <h2 class="max-w-2xl text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink leading-tight">Applied AI, not speculative AI.</h2>
    <p class="mt-5 max-w-2xl text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
      The goal is simple: reduce manual work and make systems easier to operate and understand.
    </p>
    <div class="mt-10 grid gap-8 md:grid-cols-2 md:gap-12">
      <div>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink">Event-driven workflows</h3>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
          Operational events should trigger downstream actions, not depend on manual handoffs.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink">Workflow orchestration</h3>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
          Tools like n8n are useful when integrated into clear system design with defined inputs, outputs, and failure paths.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink">AI-assisted workflows</h3>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
          Practical AI work: summarization, classification, routing, operational explanation, and workflow insight.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink">Analytics explanation</h3>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
          Systems should not just produce data. They should explain what changed and why.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink">Decision support</h3>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
          Better systems lead to faster and more informed decisions. That is the outcome.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <ToolingStack />

  <section class="grid gap-12 md:grid-cols-2">
    <article class="border-t border-line pt-8">
      <p class="mb-3 text-xs font-mono uppercase tracking-widest text-ink-soft">Selected proof</p>
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink">A smaller set of work with enough substance to evaluate.</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
        I would rather show fewer projects with real constraints, system design decisions, and operational shape than a long list of shallow summaries.
      </p>
      <ul class="mt-5 space-y-3 pl-5 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink list-disc marker:text-line">
        {featuredWork.data.highlights.map((item) => <li>{item}</li>)}
      </ul>
      <div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap gap-4">
        <a href={`/work/${featuredWork.id.replace(/\.md$/, '')}`} class="inline-flex border border-line px-5 py-2.5 text-sm font-medium text-ink no-underline hover:border-ink hover:text-ink transition-colors">Read project details</a>
        {featuredWork.data.liveUrl && (
          <a href={featuredWork.data.liveUrl} class="inline-flex border border-line px-5 py-2.5 text-sm font-medium text-ink no-underline hover:border-ink hover:text-ink transition-colors">Visit live site</a>
        )}
      </div>
    </article>

    <article class="border-t border-line pt-8">
      <p class="mb-3 text-xs font-mono uppercase tracking-widest text-ink-soft">What you will find here</p>
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink">This site shows what I build, how I think about systems, and how automation and AI fit into real engineering work.</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
        The point is signal: real constraints, real system choices, and work that holds up outside a portfolio context.
      </p>
      <ul class="mt-6 divide-y divide-line text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink">
        <li class="py-3"><strong class="font-medium text-ink">Now:</strong> what I am actively building</li>
        <li class="py-3"><strong class="font-medium text-ink">Work:</strong> selected projects with enough detail to judge scope and execution</li>
        <li class="py-3"><strong class="font-medium text-ink">Workflow:</strong> how I structure engineering, automation, and AI without losing control of the system</li>
      </ul>
    </article>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>
